    {
      "id": "claim_1deb42e95d284fb399ef3870de98b835",
      "statement": "Vulkan Scheduler::Flush submits execution and allocates a new context without waiting for the submitted work to complete. Finish waits on the pre-submit tick before allocating a new context. WaitWorker drains scheduler-side work, which is a different boundary from waiting for the device tick.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/video_core/renderer_vulkan/vk_scheduler.cpp#L62-L103",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:189f16a521c9d4f100a9f8cdb243e96a7a858409d3e7d9f26a48c7e7583d9462:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_284356e18b4c4ed0af4cb7cc52b99b8e",
      "statement": "PresentManager can queue the frame from a recorded scheduler callback when the present thread is enabled. Otherwise it waits for the scheduler worker, copies to the swapchain on the calling path, and returns the frame to the free queue. A blocked presentation should be investigated in this path after confirming composition reached Present.",
      "evidence": [
